---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import {
  SearchDialogCalendar,
  SearchDialogPlayground,
  SearchDialogRecords,
} from "../../components/SearchDialogDemo";
---

<Docs
  title="Search Dialog"
  description="A wide search palette with grouped results, filters, empty states, and keyboard hints."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Search Dialog</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A search palette pinned near the top of the screen. You filter the results;
    it groups them with counts, moves through them with the arrow keys, and
    opens the active one with Enter.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8 search-dialog-demo" id="search-dialog-demo">
    <SearchDialogPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Search Dialog usage"
      code={`import {
  SearchDialog,
  SearchEmpty,
  SearchFooter,
  SearchGroup,
  SearchHint,
  SearchInput,
  SearchItem,
  SearchItemIcon,
  SearchList,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/search-dialog";

<SearchDialog
  open={open}
  onOpenChange={setOpen}
  title="Jump to…"
  description="Find workspace pages and quick actions."
>
  <SearchInput
    ref={inputRef}
    value={query}
    onValueChange={setQuery}
    placeholder="Find a page or action…"
    label="Find a page or action"
  />
  <SearchList label="Pages and actions">
    {pages.length ? (
      <SearchGroup heading="Pages" count={pages.length}>
        {pages.map((page) => (
          <SearchItem
            key={page.id}
            value={page.id}
            title={page.title}
            media={<SearchItemIcon><page.icon size={14} aria-hidden="true" /></SearchItemIcon>}
            onSelect={() => open(page)}
          />
        ))}
      </SearchGroup>
    ) : (
      <SearchEmpty
        title="No pages or actions found"
        description="Try another page or action name."
        action={<Button variant="outline" size="sm" onClick={clear}>Clear search</Button>}
      />
    )}
  </SearchList>
  <SearchFooter>
    <SearchHint keys="↑↓">Select</SearchHint>
    <SearchHint keys="↵">Open</SearchHint>
    <SearchHint keys="Esc">Close</SearchHint>
  </SearchFooter>
</SearchDialog>`}
    />
    <p>
      Search Dialog does not filter. Match the query yourself and render only
      the results, then show <code>SearchEmpty</code> when nothing is left. Clear
      the query when the dialog closes. Give every <code>SearchItem</code> a
      <code>value</code> that is unique across groups, such as the group name plus
      the id when one entry appears under Recent and Pages.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="calendar-commands">
    <h2 class="section-title">Commands and events</h2>
    <p>
      Pass a shortcut letter as <code>trailing</code>; on the active row it
      swaps for the Enter key. <code>media</code> can be a bare icon, centered in
      a 28px box, or a muted <code>SearchItemIcon</code>. <code>detail</code>
      adds a second line such as a time. A group whose <code>count</code> is 0 is
      not rendered, and long titles truncate.
    </p>
    <SearchDialogCalendar client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="filters">
    <h2 class="section-title">Filters, meta, and empty media</h2>
    <p>
      <code>SearchFilters</code> holds a row of <code>SearchFilter</code> toggles
      that scrolls sideways when narrow. <code>meta</code> sits after the title behind
      a dot. Give <code>SearchEmpty</code> one to three icons as
      <code>media</code> to show them as fanned tiles over a faint grid.
    </p>
    <SearchDialogRecords client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="search-dialog-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <p>
      <code>SearchDialog</code> takes <code>open</code>, <code
        >onOpenChange</code
      >, a visually hidden <code>title</code> and <code>description</code>, plus
      <code>className</code> and <code>container</code>. It is 42rem wide from
      640px and pins 12% from the top. <code>SearchInput</code> takes a controlled
      <code>value</code> and <code>onValueChange</code>,
      <code>placeholder</code>, <code>label</code>, <code>closeLabel</code>, and
      a
      <code>ref</code> so a Clear search button can refocus it.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>SearchFilters</code> takes <code>label</code>; <code
        >SearchFilter</code
      >
      takes <code>pressed</code>, <code>onPressedChange</code>, and an optional
      <code>icon</code>. <code>SearchList</code> takes <code>label</code> and keeps
      a steady height. <code>SearchGroup</code> takes <code>heading</code> and
      <code>count</code>. <code>SearchItem</code> takes <code>value</code>,
      <code>onSelect</code>, <code>media</code>, <code>title</code>, and
      optional
      <code>meta</code>, <code>detail</code>, and <code>trailing</code>.
      <code>SearchEmpty</code> takes <code>title</code>, <code>description</code
      >, and optional <code>media</code> and <code>action</code>.
      <code>SearchFooter</code> holds <code>SearchHint</code>s, each with
      <code>keys</code>; it hides below 640px. Every part sets a
      <code>data-slot</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Focus moves to the search field, a <code>combobox</code> that controls the results
      <code>listbox</code>, and the active result is announced through
      <code>aria-activedescendant</code>. Arrow keys move and wrap at the ends,
      Home and End jump, Alt with arrows jumps between groups, and Enter opens.
      Group names include their count. Filters are toggle buttons with
      <code>aria-pressed</code>. The empty state is a status, so its message is
      announced. Escape or the close button closes the dialog and returns focus
      to the trigger.
    </p>
    <p>
      The dialog fades and scales over 180ms, and highlights and filters change
      over 120ms. Motion stops when reduced motion is requested.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Search Dialog uses <code>--sprout-surface</code>, <code
        >--sprout-canvas</code
      >,
      <code>--sprout-text</code>, <code>--sprout-muted</code>,
      <code>--sprout-line</code>, <code>--sprout-input</code>,
      <code>--sprout-hover</code>, <code>--sprout-active</code>,
      <code>--sprout-focus</code>, <code>--sprout-overlay</code>, and the panel
      shadows and radii. It needs no brand color, so it looks the same with the
      neutral and TulipFarm themes in light and dark mode.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
